# Shell scripts must always be checked out with LF endings.
#
# The Docker image runs scripts/docker-entrypoint.sh as its CMD. With CRLF
# endings the kernel reads the shebang as "/bin/bash\r", fails to find that
# interpreter, and the container dies immediately with exit 127:
#
#   exec: /app/scripts/docker-entrypoint.sh: not found
#
# Git stores these blobs with LF, but a clone made with core.autocrlf=true
# (the Git for Windows default) converts them on checkout and produces a
# broken image. Forcing eol=lf here makes the checkout platform-independent.
*.sh text eol=lf
